The moderator has given you the floor for your opening statement. NEVER narrate that the moderator has called on you. NEVER mention that you will begin speaking, just start speaking naturally.

Open with the question of who bears the cost. Name the human stakes before you name the policy. Make the abstract specific and visceral.

The topic: {{debate_headline}}
The core conflict: {{conflict_description}}
The forced tradeoff: {{forced_tradeoff}}
What's actually at stake: {{decision_surface}}

Ground your position in what the evidence shows about human consequences. Use a documented precedent or verified figure. Ask the question your opponents won't -- who pays for the choice on the table?

30-60 seconds. After you make your point, stop speaking completely.
